  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-26: "Yes, start group C" (deferred-issue triage group C, notes/deferred-triage-2026-11.md). Read gh issue view 1697. Dataverse appnotification accepts priority 200000000 / 200000001 and toasttype 200000000 / 200000001. On origin/master d43fc9e16d GrantExpiryReminderJob.cs:99 (PriorityCritical = 200000002) and IncomingCommunicationJobHandler.cs:209 (priority: 200000002) write an invalid value, so the held-email admin alert is lost and the last-day reminder is never delivered; NotificationService.cs:47/96 documents a Critical value that does not exist. PR #1494 (branch work/132-notification-delivery-correctness, open, stale) added AppNotificationOptions (constants + Validate) and fixed these writers; re-apply its intent on a fresh branch from origin/master, dropping anything that touched the retired playbook path (CreateNotificationNodeExecutor and the retired playbook JSONs, D-100). Verify the option values from the repo solution source or by a read-only metadata read; never write.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse option sets, ADR-004/036 jobs.</role>
  <goal>Every appnotification the BFF writes uses a valid priority and toast type, so the held-email alert and the last-day grant reminder are delivered as High.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Keep NotificationService's contract for existing callers; an invalid value passed in throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException before any write. Run /conflict-check (NotificationService is shared).</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run the relevant --filter (Signals code: "FullyQualifiedName~Signals", which includes the contract baselines; Communication: "FullyQualifiedName~Communication"; Ai: "FullyQualifiedName~Ai"); update any baseline the change moves in the same PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene when the BFF changes: publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface, endpoint or DI registration unless the three questions are answered in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests (build tests/Spaarke.ArchTests explicitly first). Client code: run node scripts/quality/client-lint/client-lint.mjs check and the package jest suite.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment GUIDs, user or contact ids, mailbox addresses, tenant names or private access-control mechanics in code, tests, notes, commits or the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §2 / D-106">Fix only what the named issues describe. Any other defect found: report it in the task notes and to the main session; do not fix it here.</constraint>
  </constraints>
